\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {I}{\ignorespaces Combined primordial-power model and cosmological \(N\)-body simulation parameters. The \(k_p\) and \(m_s\) columns specify the PL/BT primordial power-spectrum template, while \(N_{\rm  p}\), \(L_{\rm  box}\), \(m_{\rm  DM}\), and \(\epsilon _{\rm  Pl}\) specify the numerical realization. The main comparison uses the matched PL, BT\_soft, and BT\_deep \(25\,h^{-1}{\rm  Mpc}\), \(1024^3\) runs. Additional BT and PL runs provide numerical checks. Here \(m_{\rm  DM}\) is measured from the snapshot mass table, and \(\epsilon _{\rm  Pl}\) is the Plummer-equivalent softening length in physical kpc at \(z=0\).}}{4}{table.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:simulation_parameters}{{I}{4}{Combined primordial-power model and cosmological \(N\)-body simulation parameters. The \(k_p\) and \(m_s\) columns specify the PL/BT primordial power-spectrum template, while \(N_{\rm p}\), \(L_{\rm box}\), \(m_{\rm DM}\), and \(\epsilon _{\rm Pl}\) specify the numerical realization. The main comparison uses the matched PL, BT\_soft, and BT\_deep \(25\,h^{-1}{\rm Mpc}\), \(1024^3\) runs. Additional BT and PL runs provide numerical checks. Here \(m_{\rm DM}\) is measured from the snapshot mass table, and \(\epsilon _{\rm Pl}\) is the Plummer-equivalent softening length in physical kpc at \(z=0\)}{table.1}{}}
\newlabel{tab:Params_all_models}{{I}{4}{Combined primordial-power model and cosmological \(N\)-body simulation parameters. The \(k_p\) and \(m_s\) columns specify the PL/BT primordial power-spectrum template, while \(N_{\rm p}\), \(L_{\rm box}\), \(m_{\rm DM}\), and \(\epsilon _{\rm Pl}\) specify the numerical realization. The main comparison uses the matched PL, BT\_soft, and BT\_deep \(25\,h^{-1}{\rm Mpc}\), \(1024^3\) runs. Additional BT and PL runs provide numerical checks. Here \(m_{\rm DM}\) is measured from the snapshot mass table, and \(\epsilon _{\rm Pl}\) is the Plummer-equivalent softening length in physical kpc at \(z=0\)}{table.1}{}}
