\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Direct particle radial density profiles for PL, BT\_soft, and BT\_deep halos in four \(M_{200m}\) bins. Open symbols show the median particle-count radial density profiles for \(N=100\) halos per model and mass bin, where available. Error bars and shaded ratio bands show bootstrap 16th--84th percentile intervals for the median stacks and BT/PL ratios. Dashed curves show Diemer et al. NFW reference profiles for the corresponding PL and BT models \citep  {Diemer2019}. These dashed curves are reference profiles, not fits to the particle stacks. The gray shaded radial range and vertical dotted line mark the Power03 convergence criterion, labelled by \(\kappa =0.6\). Lower panels show the BT/PL profile ratios in the same bins. The \(10^8\,M_\odot \) panel is closest to the resolution boundary and is interpreted qualitatively; the higher-mass panels show that the BT\_soft enhancement is largest in the inner resolved profile and weakens toward \(R_{200m}\).}}{11}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:halo_density_analysis}{{7}{11}{Direct particle radial density profiles for PL, BT\_soft, and BT\_deep halos in four \(M_{200m}\) bins. Open symbols show the median particle-count radial density profiles for \(N=100\) halos per model and mass bin, where available. Error bars and shaded ratio bands show bootstrap 16th--84th percentile intervals for the median stacks and BT/PL ratios. Dashed curves show Diemer et al. NFW reference profiles for the corresponding PL and BT models \citep {Diemer2019}. These dashed curves are reference profiles, not fits to the particle stacks. The gray shaded radial range and vertical dotted line mark the Power03 convergence criterion, labelled by \(\kappa =0.6\). Lower panels show the BT/PL profile ratios in the same bins. The \(10^8\,M_\odot \) panel is closest to the resolution boundary and is interpreted qualitatively; the higher-mass panels show that the BT\_soft enhancement is largest in the inner resolved profile and weakens toward \(R_{200m}\)}{figure.7}{}}
