\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Concentration--mass relations for the PL, BT\_soft ($k_p=1\,h\,{\rm  Mpc}^{-1}$, $m_s=1.5$), and BT\_deep ($k_p=10\,h\,{\rm  Mpc}^{-1}$, $m_s=1.5$) models at four representative redshifts. Symbols show the simulation measurements and curves show the corresponding semi-analytic predictions. Simulation points require \(N_{\rm  DM}\ge 100\), corresponding to \(M_{200c}\gtrsim 1.9\times 10^8\,M_\odot \). The gray shaded region marks the low-particle-number structural caution range. Quantitative low-mass concentration claims are quoted near and above \(10^9\,M_\odot \). At $z=0$, the median concentration in the $10^9$--$10^{9.5}\,M_\odot $ bin is higher than PL by factors of $3.20$ and $1.35$ for the $k_p=1$ and $k_p=10$ runs, respectively.}}{13}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:concentration_comparison}{{8}{13}{Concentration--mass relations for the PL, BT\_soft ($k_p=1\,h\,{\rm Mpc}^{-1}$, $m_s=1.5$), and BT\_deep ($k_p=10\,h\,{\rm Mpc}^{-1}$, $m_s=1.5$) models at four representative redshifts. Symbols show the simulation measurements and curves show the corresponding semi-analytic predictions. Simulation points require \(N_{\rm DM}\ge 100\), corresponding to \(M_{200c}\gtrsim 1.9\times 10^8\,M_\odot \). The gray shaded region marks the low-particle-number structural caution range. Quantitative low-mass concentration claims are quoted near and above \(10^9\,M_\odot \). At $z=0$, the median concentration in the $10^9$--$10^{9.5}\,M_\odot $ bin is higher than PL by factors of $3.20$ and $1.35$ for the $k_p=1$ and $k_p=10$ runs, respectively}{figure.8}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {B}Relation to Previous Work}{13}{section*.23}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Nonlinear matter power spectra and matched BT/PL response ratios at representative redshifts. The upper panels show PL and BT spectra for the \(k_p=1\) and \(k_p=10\), \(m_s=1.5\) variants in the matched \(25\) and \(256\,h^{-1}{\rm  Mpc}\) boxes, together with the corresponding HMcode2020 nonlinear theory curves computed with \texttt  {pyhmcode} for orientation. The theory curves use the same PL or BT input linear spectra described in the text and are not fitted to the simulation measurements. The lower panels show the direct simulation ratios BT/PL for each matched box and \(k_p\), plus the corresponding BT-theory/PL-theory ratios. In the fiducial $k_p=1$, $25\,h^{-1}{\rm  Mpc}$ box at $z=0$, BT/PL reaches $1.17$ at $k=20\,h\,{\rm  Mpc}^{-1}$ and $1.34$ at $k=40\,h\,{\rm  Mpc}^{-1}$. The spectra are measured on \(1024^3\) meshes. Vertical markers show the mesh Nyquist scales for the \(256\) and \(25\,h^{-1}{\rm  Mpc}\) boxes. Quantitative interpretation of the \(256\,h^{-1}{\rm  Mpc}\) comparison is restricted to \(k\le k_{\rm  Ny}\simeq 12.6\,h\,{\rm  Mpc}^{-1}\). The fiducial 25-box high-\(k\) points remain below its mesh Nyquist frequency \(k_{\rm  Ny}\simeq 129\,h\,{\rm  Mpc}^{-1}\), but they are used only as checks of the small-scale trend because their amplitude is sensitive to the power-spectrum estimator. The gray high-\(k\) region marks scales beyond the 25-box Nyquist frequency, and the shaded band around unity in the ratio panels marks a \(\pm 10\%\) reference interval.}}{14}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:power_spectra_ratio_z0}{{9}{14}{Nonlinear matter power spectra and matched BT/PL response ratios at representative redshifts. The upper panels show PL and BT spectra for the \(k_p=1\) and \(k_p=10\), \(m_s=1.5\) variants in the matched \(25\) and \(256\,h^{-1}{\rm Mpc}\) boxes, together with the corresponding HMcode2020 nonlinear theory curves computed with \texttt {pyhmcode} for orientation. The theory curves use the same PL or BT input linear spectra described in the text and are not fitted to the simulation measurements. The lower panels show the direct simulation ratios BT/PL for each matched box and \(k_p\), plus the corresponding BT-theory/PL-theory ratios. In the fiducial $k_p=1$, $25\,h^{-1}{\rm Mpc}$ box at $z=0$, BT/PL reaches $1.17$ at $k=20\,h\,{\rm Mpc}^{-1}$ and $1.34$ at $k=40\,h\,{\rm Mpc}^{-1}$. The spectra are measured on \(1024^3\) meshes. Vertical markers show the mesh Nyquist scales for the \(256\) and \(25\,h^{-1}{\rm Mpc}\) boxes. Quantitative interpretation of the \(256\,h^{-1}{\rm Mpc}\) comparison is restricted to \(k\le k_{\rm Ny}\simeq 12.6\,h\,{\rm Mpc}^{-1}\). The fiducial 25-box high-\(k\) points remain below its mesh Nyquist frequency \(k_{\rm Ny}\simeq 129\,h\,{\rm Mpc}^{-1}\), but they are used only as checks of the small-scale trend because their amplitude is sensitive to the power-spectrum estimator. The gray high-\(k\) region marks scales beyond the 25-box Nyquist frequency, and the shaded band around unity in the ratio panels marks a \(\pm 10\%\) reference interval}{figure.9}{}}
